# scripts/leak-patterns.local.template — template for .leak-patterns.local
#
# .leak-patterns.local lives at the REPOSITORY ROOT and is never committed
# (it is in .gitignore). It is the operator's own list of machine-specific
# tokens — a personal hostname, an internal registry host, a kubectl
# context name, a private Wi-Fi SSID, etc. — that are too private to put
# in the checked-in scripts/leak-check.patterns.
#
# Format:
#   - one fixed-string pattern per line
#   - matching is case-insensitive substring matching, against every
#     scanned file, and the matched text is never printed — only
#     "path:line: local"
#   - blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored
#
# If the file is absent or holds only comments and blank lines, the check
# prints "local patterns: skipped" and carries on — that is never an
# error. The 'local' class is the only one fed by this file.
#
# `make leak-patterns-init` (scripts/seed-leak-patterns.sh) creates the real
# file from this template when it is absent and automatically appends the
# names the local datawatch daemon knows — federation peers, compute nodes,
# observer peers and pool hosts — one per line beneath a dedicated comment
# marker, deduplicated against existing lines case-insensitively (remember
# that matching itself is case-insensitive substring matching). An existing
# file is never overwritten. Only a count is printed; names are not.
#
# To create the real file by hand:
#   copy this file to ".leak-patterns.local" at the repository root and
#   add your patterns there. Do not commit the result.
